{"name":"Catalina Tile","hex":"#efac73","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A regularly-shaped slab of clay or other material, affixed to cover or decorate a surface, as in a roof-tile, glazed tile, stove tile, carpet tile, etc.","A rectangular graphic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with tiles.","To arrange in a regular pattern, with adjoining edges (applied to tile-like objects, graphics, windows in a computer interface)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tile"}],"entries":[{"title":"Catalina Pottery","blocks":[{"text":"Catalina Pottery is the commonly used name for Catalina Clay Products, a division of the Santa Catalina Island Company, which produced brick, tile, tableware and decorative pottery on Santa Catalina Island, California. Catalina Clay Products was founded in 1927. Gladding, McBean & Co. acquired all of the assets of the company in 1937 and moved all production to its Franciscan dinnerware division in Los Angeles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Catalina_pottery_oil_jar.jpg/330px-Catalina_pottery_oil_jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catalina_Pottery","wikidata":"Q5051274"},{"title":"Tile","blocks":[{"text":"Tiles are usually thin, square rectangular coverings manufactured from hard-wearing material such as ceramic, stone, metal, baked clay, or even glass. They are generally fixed in place in an array to cover roofs, floors, walls, edges, or other objects such as tabletops. Alternatively, tile can sometimes refer to similar units made from lightweight materials such as perlite, wood, and mineral wool, typically used for wall and ceiling applications. In another sense, a tile is a construction tile or similar object, such as rectangular counters used in playing games. The word is derived from the French word tuile, which is, in turn, from the Latin word tegula, meaning a roof tile composed of fired clay, otherwise known as nga."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg/330px-Alban_chambon%2C_decorazione_in_marmo_e_ceramica%2C_dal_castello_reale_delle_ardenne%2C_houyet%2C_1905_ca._02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tile","wikidata":"Q468402"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Catalina_pottery_green_vase.jpg/500px-Catalina_pottery_green_vase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Catalina_pottery_green_vase.jpg/500px-Catalina_pottery_green_vase.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Catalina Pottery vase","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatalina_pottery_green_vase.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg/500px-Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg/1280px-Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg/500px-Catalina_pottery_plate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Catalina Pottery painted plate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatalina_pottery_plate.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Art_Nouveau_tiles_in_the_house_with_number_6%2C_Strada_Speran%C8%9Bei%2C_Bucharest_%28Romania%29.jpg/500px-Art_Nouveau_tiles_in_the_house_with_number_6%2C_Strada_S